{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# The `(inbound, probe)` dispatch chain is a documented subsystem with no live producer\n\n## Status\n\nDISCOVERED while fixing d103-c3f8-2fbc-4c97 / 727f-b351-59ba-4b3b. Not a regression those\nfixes introduced - it predates them and neither changes it. Filed so it is not lost.\n\n## What is unreachable\n\n`differ._compute_mutations_emit_absent_partner_probes` is the only producer of\n`(inbound, probe)` mutations. It iterates `local_state` looking for entries carrying a\nbound `jira_key` field. Its sole production caller, `run_differs`, passes\n`prev_snapshot` - a FETCHED Jira snapshot, whose entries never carry `jira_key`\n(`fetcher.py`, and the contract shape in `_snapshot_schema.py`). The loop therefore never\nemits, and everything downstream of it is dead in production:\n\n* `_run_differs_inbound_probe_dispatch` in `run_differs.py`\n* `inbound_probe.py` (`ProbeResult`, `ProbeBranch`, the router)\n* `backend.probe_remote` / the `SupportsAbsenceProbe` capability\n\nConfirmed empirically: fed a realistic fetched-snapshot pair, `compute_mutations` emits only\n`jira_new`, `unbound_local` and `field_drift`. The only fixture in the repo that supplies a\n`jira_key`-bearing `local_state` is\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_emits_probe.py`.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThis is the mechanism ADR 0028 para 2 relies on to tell \"deleted\" from \"aged out of the fetch\nwindow\" - deletion is proven only by a bounded direct GET returning 404. With no live producer,\nthat discrimination is never exercised in production. Ticket b9b8 already reworked the live DC\ncell `test_a_deleted_dc_issue_is_planned_as_an_inbound_probe` for exactly this reason: it\n\"asserted an observable no production path emits\".\n\n## What is NOT the fix\n\nDo NOT re-enable the arm by making `run_differs` pass a `jira_key`-bearing local_state without\nalso removing `reconcile_helpers.drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions` in the SAME change.\nThat suppression exists only because the caller passes the legacy `(prev, curr)` pair; migrating\nthe caller makes the suppressed emissions correct again, and leaving both in place would silently\ndrop real work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Establish whether the absence-probe path is still wanted, or whether ADR 0028 para 2's\n      direct-GET confirmation has since been implemented elsewhere. **ANSWERED** — implemented twice\n      and both live: `outbound_differ._safe_get_issue` (L13) and `binding_walk.py:187-196` (ADR para 4),\n      called at `run_differs.py:222` / `:257`. Verified live on DC: Row 14\n      `test_a_deleted_dc_issue_never_plans_a_local_teardown` PASSED in harness run 30933704255.\n- [x] ~~a RED-first test proving `(inbound, probe)` is produced from the real production call path~~ —\n      **MOOT** under the operator ruling; no producer is to be created.\n- [ ] the dead chain is removed: `differ._compute_mutations_emit_absent_partner_probes`,\n      `_run_differs_inbound_probe_dispatch`, `route_inbound_probe`, and the fixture-only\n      `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_emits_probe.py`\n- [ ] RED-first: a local ticket whose binding was retired on a confirmed 404 gets NO outbound create —\n      the test FAILS before the guard exists and PASSES after, checked by running it at both commits\n- [ ] a never-bound local ticket STILL gets its outbound create, asserted in the same test module so\n      the guard cannot suppress ordinary creation\n- [ ] the suppression is observable (bridge alert or sync-log line) naming the local id and the retired\n      key, and the message states the escape hatch for an operator who does want a fresh issue\n- [ ] `BindingStore.is_retired_local(local_id)` tolerates legacy/duck-typed stores the way\n      `outbound_differ._is_retired` does — asserted with a stub store lacking the method\n- [ ] ADR 0028's c244 Consequence is corrected to describe tombstone semantics\n- [ ] `drop_snapshot_differ_local_state_emissions` is still present and still consulted — asserted, so\n      the WIRE trap cannot be entered by accident\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler -q                    # the reconciler tier\n    pytest tests/unit -q                                     # full unit suite (no regressions)\n    make lint && make typecheck\n\nThe RED-first proof for the tombstone guard is run explicitly at two commits: the test is added\nfirst and must FAIL against the pre-guard tree, then PASS once the guard lands. A guard asserted\nwithout a demonstrated RED is unverified, and this one suppresses work — the failure mode of a\nwrong guard is silently not creating issues, which no green suite would surface.\n\nRemoval of the dead chain is proved by the suite continuing to pass with the producer, the dispatch\narm and the router gone — plus a grep confirming no remaining `(inbound, probe)` producer, since the\ndynamic loader means an import-graph check alone would miss a string-loaded module."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785870265497513001,"uuid":"c60fa765-46db-4d79-8a9e-e633ce95078e"}